+- **A gate records the toolchain version before and after and refuses a verdict when it changed (experiment; card 418 retro, Decider D251).** While this entry is on trial: every facilitator baseline gate and every sign-off run prints `dotnet --version` (and the versions of the other toolchains the run uses, such as `python --version`) before the run and again after it, into the gate summary or the sign-off reply; if a version differs, or a folder of the toolchain changed during the run, the verdict of that run is void: it is not recorded as a pass or a failure of the card, its logs are kept with a note, and the run is repeated on the new toolchain; the gate script prints the two lines; the independent gate reviewer checks the stamp in the gate records.
+  - Hypothesis: an environment update during a run is not scored as a card failure, and no contaminated verdict is accepted. Metric: gate verdicts accepted although the toolchain changed during the run (card 418: 1, a .NET SDK update installed mid-gate gave 13 simultaneous failures, found by reading timestamps and one error), target 0. Counter-metric: seconds added per gate (target under 5) and benign version-string changes that void a run. Trial: the next 3 cards with a baseline gate, counted from Decider D251. Owner: the facilitator. Review at the third card's retro: keep, change or remove.
